        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There are still <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39393#issuecomment-2851420219\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/39393/hovercard\">several Learn articles</a> not linked from the learnsidebar. The ones we want to keep should really be linked in some way. This PR provides an experimental suggestion of what we could do in each case — an \"Additional tutorials\" subsection at the end of each module sidebar subsection.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41196",
            "title": "[Experiment]: Add CSS layout additional tutorials links to learnsidebar",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-18T15:52:06.000Z",
